},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows database_sql.go and lists the original authors by name, but gives no shares and doesn't name Overfelt as the largest author. It mentions Ravi's rename only as a recent change.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Recommends Ravi, Alexander Rowe and Sam Okafor as active. It gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It doesn't mention Kofi.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Lists Noor Haddad as a recent maintainer-type contributor and Sam Okafor as a second reviewer for time.go, so both are treated as experts.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Gives Paul Borman 70.9% (73.0% with blank lines), which is in range, and calls him inactive. But it says his last commit was 2016, and the ground truth says 2023, and it didn't merge his identities. It also handles Sam Okafor's line-ending commit correctly. The main-author and inactive points mostly hold, but the last-commit date is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"MikeWang 81.2% and Mei Chen 9.4–9.7% are both given. Mei is credited with Time7 although Ravi committed it, and Ravi is held at 2 lines (1.9%), under 5%.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows database_sql.go back to sql.go and names Justin Overfelt as top author at 44.1% (39.6% non-blank), with Stone and Wheeler. It omits Daniel Souza by name, saying only 'six authors', and all are inactive. Ravi is not credited. Overall this is acceptable.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It doesn't give the repo-wide share of lines owned by departed people. It lists Alex Rowe as the only active person and doesn't merge Alexander Rowe, so Alex is left as ambiguous or split. It doesn't mention Ravi and Kofi as active in the repo overall.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Handles Sam Okafor's line-ending commit correctly and doesn't credit Noor. It doesn't mention Kofi Mensah or the bot commits.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Gives only commit counts and says Borman hasn't